+config ROCKCHIP_SUSPEND_MODE
+	bool "Rockchip BSP suspend-mode policy core"
+	depends on ARM64 && ARCH_ROCKCHIP && OF && REGULATOR && SUSPEND
+	help
+	  Build the strict Rockchip BSP suspend policy parser, typed sequence
+	  model, generic executor, and narrow hardware backend.  With activation
+	  disabled, the driver accepts only a policy-free node and performs no
+	  firmware, regulator, CPU, PSCI, or MMIO actions.
+
+config ROCKCHIP_SUSPEND_MODE_ACTIVATE
+	bool "Activate the Rockchip BSP suspend-mode policy (issues SIP calls)"
+	depends on ROCKCHIP_SUSPEND_MODE
+	default n
+	help
+	  Link the callback-registration and executor-call edge, and accept a
+	  policy-bearing rockchip-suspend node.  With this set the driver DOES
+	  issue firmware SIP calls and program regulator suspend state; with it
+	  unset the driver binds only a metadata-only node and touches nothing.
+
+	  This is REQUIRED for platform `deep` suspend on RK356x.  Without it
+	  firmware receives no suspend-mode configuration and no wake-source
+	  arming, and the system will not wake: measured on PineNote
+	  2026-08-02, bl31 reported
+	  `PM-STATE: mem (ultra: 0, mem: 1, cfg: 0x0)` and never returned.
+
+	  Do not set this unless the platform's policy values have been
+	  verified against a known-working configuration for that exact device,
+	  and the emitted SIP sequence has been differentially checked against
+	  the BSP emitter.  Both were done for the PineNote — see
+	  doc/artifacts/pinenote-os1-suspend-policy-20260802/ and
+	  doc/artifacts/pinenote-sip-sequence-differential-20260802.md.
+
 endif
